inking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The retry returned PO0002 with the full order. PO0001 may now duplicate the docks, so I'll check the order list before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NXiQpnsJk29vPXKha3kDFx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_orders", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PO0001 is a duplicate of the dock portion of PO0002, left over from the timed-out request. I'll cancel it so the docks aren't ordered twice. The cancellation refunds the $567.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Gz8d2TysqnUV3BQFYnhVS5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"order_id": "PO0001"}, "name": "cancel_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I placed one purchase order for the new hires, PO0002, shipping to HQ. It contains 3 \u00d7 DK-200 USB-C docks and 3 \u00d7 MN-27 27-inch 4K monitors, all new (not refurbished), for a total of $1,554. That is under the $2,500 threshold, so no manager approval was needed.\n\nThe first attempt timed out, and its partial order (PO0001, the 3 docks for $567) was left in the system. The retry created PO0002 with the full order, so I cancelled PO0001 and it was refunded. The docks are therefore ordered once, and the only active order is PO0002.\n\nThe ship-to was entered as \"HQ\" because no street address was given. Please confirm that matches the address the IT team normally uses.", "type": "text"}]}]}